 "text": " Finally, when connecting multiple chips together, engineers choose the right communication wire for the job. A single GPIO pin for simple on-off switches, I2C when chaining many sensors onto just two shared wires using addresses, SPI for high-speed displays, or UART for direct serial messages. Always check the component's datasheet for its voltage limits before powering on, so you build reliable, long-lasting hardware instead of electronic waste. Now that we can build a single smart device, how do two devices talk to each other across a room or across the planet? In video 2, we will trace a message across the global network.",
